<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <title>Bylaws of {{company_name}}</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --primary-text: #111111;
      --muted-text: #555555;
      --border-color: #cccccc;
      --section-border: #e0e0e0;
      --heading-font: "Georgia", "Times New Roman", serif;
      --body-font: "Times New Roman", serif;
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 40px;
      font-family: var(--body-font);
      font-size: 12pt;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: var(--primary-text);
      background: #ffffff;
    }

    .document {
      max-width: 800px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    h1, h2, h3, h4 {
      font-family: var(--heading-font);
      margin-top: 1.2em;
      margin-bottom: 0.4em;
    }

    h1 {
      text-align: center;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 1px;
      font-size: 18pt;
    }

    h2 {
      text-align: center;
      font-size: 14pt;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    h3 {
      font-size: 12.5pt;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    h4 {
      font-size: 12pt;
      font-style: italic;
    }

    p {
      margin: 0.3em 0;
    }

    .center {
      text-align: center;
    }

    .muted {
      color: var(--muted-text);
    }

    .article {
      margin-top: 1.5em;
      padding-top: 1em;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--section-border);
      page-break-inside: avoid;
    }

    .section-title {
      font-weight: bold;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .block {
      margin-top: 0.3em;
      margin-bottom: 0.5em;
    }

    .page-break {
      page-break-before: always;
    }

    .signature-section {
      margin-top: 3em;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color);
      padding-top: 1.5em;
    }

    .signature-row {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 40px;
      margin-bottom: 40px;
    }

    .signature-block {
      flex: 1 1 220px;
      min-width: 220px;
    }

    .signature-line {
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
      height: 1.8em;
      margin-bottom: 0.2em;
    }

    .signature-label {
      font-size: 10pt;
      color: var(--muted-text);
    }

    .execution-note {
      margin-bottom: 1em;
      font-size: 10.5pt;
    }

    .meta-header {
      text-align: center;
      margin-bottom: 1em;
      font-size: 10.5pt;
      color: var(--muted-text);
    }

    .title-block {
      margin-bottom: 1.5em;
    }

    .title-block p {
      text-align: center;
      margin: 0.2em 0;
    }

    .bold {
      font-weight: bold;
    }

    ul {
      margin: 0.5em 0;
      padding-left: 2em;
    }

    li {
      margin: 0.3em 0;
    }

    @media print {
      body {
        padding: 24px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="document">
    <!-- Title / Meta -->
    <div class="title-block">
      <h1>BYLAWS</h1>
      <h2>OF</h2>
      <h2>{{uppercase company_name}}</h2>
      <p class="muted">a {{state_of_incorporation}} corporation</p>
      <p class="muted">Adopted as of {{adoption_date}}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="meta-header">
      These Bylaws govern the internal affairs and corporate governance of {{company_name}}
      (the “Corporation”), including the rights and obligations of its shareholders,
      directors, and officers, and are adopted pursuant to the Delaware General Corporation
      Law, 8 Del. C. § 101 et seq. (the “DGCL”).
    </div>

    <!-- ARTICLE I -->
    <div class="article">
      <h3>ARTICLE I – OFFICES</h3>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 1.1 Registered Office.</span>
        The registered office of {{company_name}} (hereinafter, the “Corporation”) in the State
        of {{state_of_incorporation}} shall be the office designated in the Corporation’s Certificate of
        Incorporation, as amended from time to time, or at such other location within the
        State of {{state_of_incorporation}} as the Board of Directors (the “Board”) may from time to time
        designate in accordance with applicable provisions of the DGCL. The registered agent
        at such address shall likewise be as stated in the Certificate of Incorporation or
        as otherwise appointed by the Board.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 1.2 Principal Executive Office.</span>
        The principal executive office and primary place of business of the Corporation
        shall initially be located in {{principal_office_city}}, {{principal_office_state}}, presently at {{principal_office_address}},
        or at such other place or places, within or outside the State of {{state_of_incorporation}}, as may
        from time to time be determined by resolution of the Board. The Board may designate
        additional executive, operational, or administrative offices as it deems necessary or
        appropriate for the conduct of the Corporation’s business.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 1.3 Other Offices.</span>
        The Corporation may also have such other offices, within or outside the State of
        {{state_of_incorporation}}, as the Board may from time to time determine or the business of the
        Corporation may require. The failure to maintain any such additional office shall
        not impair the corporate existence of the Corporation or the validity of any
        corporate acts taken in accordance with these Bylaws and the DGCL.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ARTICLE II -->
    <div class="article">
      <h3>ARTICLE II – CAPITAL STOCK</h3>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 2.1 Authorized Shares.</span>
        The total number of shares of stock which the Corporation shall have authority to
        issue, and the classes and series thereof, shall be as set forth in the Certificate
        of Incorporation, as the same may be amended from time to time. As of the adoption of
        these Bylaws, the Corporation is authorized to issue {{authorized_shares}}
        shares of Common Stock, par value {{par_value}} per share (“Common Stock”),
        all of which shall have the rights, powers, preferences, and limitations specified
        in the Certificate of Incorporation and applicable law.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 2.2 Consideration for Shares.</span>
        Subject to the provisions of the Certificate of Incorporation and the DGCL, shares
        of the Corporation may be issued for such lawful consideration (including, without
        limitation, cash, property, or services actually rendered to the Corporation) as
        shall be authorized from time to time by the Board. The judgment of the Board as to
        the value of the consideration received for shares shall be conclusive to the
        fullest extent permitted by law.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 2.3 Form of Shares; Certificated and Uncertificated.</span>
        Shares of the Corporation’s capital stock may be represented by certificates or may
        be issued in uncertificated form, as determined from time to time by resolution of
        the Board, subject to the requirements of the DGCL. If certificates are issued, such
        certificates shall be in such form as shall be approved by the Board and shall be
        signed by, or in the name of, the Corporation by the Chair of the Board, the Chief
        Executive Officer (“CEO”), the President (if any), or any Vice President, and by the
        Secretary or an Assistant Secretary.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 2.4 Transfer of Shares.</span>
        Transfers of shares of the Corporation shall be made only on the books of the
        Corporation by the holder of record thereof or by such holder’s duly authorized
        attorney or representative, upon (a) in the case of certificated shares, surrender
        for cancellation of certificates for the number of shares to be transferred, duly
        endorsed or accompanied by proper instruments of assignment and transfer, or (b) in
        the case of uncertificated shares, compliance with appropriate instructions and
        procedures established by the Corporation and its transfer agent, if any. All
        transfers shall be subject to such restrictions on transfer and ownership as may be
        imposed by law, the Certificate of Incorporation, these Bylaws, or any agreement
        among the shareholders and the Corporation duly approved by the Board.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 2.5 Lost, Stolen, or Destroyed Certificates.</span>
        The Corporation may issue a new share certificate in place of any certificate
        theretofore issued which is alleged to have been lost, stolen, or destroyed, upon
        such terms and conditions as the Board may require, including, without limitation,
        the furnishing of an affidavit of loss and an indemnity bond in form and substance
        satisfactory to the Corporation.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ARTICLE III -->
    <div class="article page-break">
      <h3>ARTICLE III – MEETINGS OF SHAREHOLDERS</h3>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 3.1 Place of Meetings.</span>
        Meetings of the shareholders shall be held at such place, within or outside the State
        of {{state_of_incorporation}}, as may from time to time be designated by the Board and stated in the
        notice of such meeting. The Board may, in its sole discretion, determine that any
        meeting of shareholders shall be held solely by means of remote communication in the
        manner authorized by the DGCL.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 3.2 Annual Meetings.</span>
        An annual meeting of shareholders for the election of directors and for the
        transaction of such other proper business as may come before the meeting shall be
        held each year on such date and at such time as may be fixed by resolution of the
        Board. Failure to hold the annual meeting at the designated time or to transact any
        business at such meeting shall not work a forfeiture or dissolution of the
        Corporation and shall not affect otherwise valid corporate acts.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 3.3 Special Meetings.</span>
        Special meetings of the shareholders may be called at any time and for any proper
        purpose or purposes by (a) the Board, (b) the Chair of the Board, or (c) the CEO.
        Shareholders shall not be entitled to call a special meeting of shareholders unless
        expressly authorized to do so in the Certificate of Incorporation. Any such special
        meeting shall be held at such date, time, and place as shall be fixed by the person
        or body calling such meeting and stated in the notice thereof.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 3.4 Notice of Meetings.</span>
        Written notice of each meeting of shareholders, whether annual or special, stating
        the date, time, and place (or means of remote communication, if any) of the meeting,
        and, in the case of a special meeting, the purpose or purposes for which the meeting
        is called, shall be given not less than ten (10) nor more than sixty (60) days before
        the date of the meeting to each shareholder entitled to vote thereat, except to the
        extent that a longer or shorter period of notice may be required by the DGCL or the
        Certificate of Incorporation.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 3.5 Quorum.</span>
        Except as otherwise provided by law, the Certificate of Incorporation, or these
        Bylaws, the holders of a majority of the shares of the Corporation entitled to vote
        at any meeting of shareholders, present in person or represented by proxy, shall
        constitute a quorum for the transaction of business thereat. If, however, such
        quorum shall not be present or represented at any meeting of shareholders, the
        holders of a majority of the shares so present or represented may adjourn the
        meeting from time to time, without further notice, until a quorum shall be present
        or represented.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 3.6 Voting.</span>
        Except as otherwise provided by the DGCL, the Certificate of Incorporation, or these
        Bylaws, each outstanding share of Common Stock shall entitle the holder thereof to
        one (1) vote on each matter submitted to a vote of shareholders. Except as otherwise
        required by law, the Certificate of Incorporation, or these Bylaws, the affirmative
        vote of a majority of the shares present in person or represented by proxy at a
        meeting at which a quorum is present and entitled to vote shall be the act of the
        shareholders.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 3.7 Proxies.</span>
        Each shareholder entitled to vote at a meeting of shareholders may authorize another
        person or persons to act for such shareholder by proxy, which shall be given in
        writing or by electronic transmission as permitted by the DGCL. Every proxy shall be
        revocable unless expressly stated to be irrevocable in compliance with applicable law.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 3.8 Action by Written Consent.</span>
        Unless otherwise provided in the Certificate of Incorporation, any action required or
        permitted to be taken at a meeting of shareholders may be taken without a meeting,
        without prior notice, and without a vote, if a consent or consents in writing, setting
        forth the action so taken, shall be signed by the holders of outstanding shares
        having not less than the minimum number of votes that would be necessary to authorize
        or take such action at a meeting at which all shares entitled to vote thereon were
        present and voted, all in accordance with the DGCL.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ARTICLE IV -->
    <div class="article">
      <h3>ARTICLE IV – BOARD OF DIRECTORS</h3>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 4.1 General Powers.</span>
        The business and affairs of the Corporation shall be managed and controlled by or
        under the direction of the Board, which shall exercise all such powers of the
        Corporation and do all such lawful acts and things as are not, by the DGCL, the
        Certificate of Incorporation, or these Bylaws, directed or required to be exercised
        or done by the shareholders.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 4.2 Number and Qualifications of Directors.</span>
        The number of directors that shall constitute the whole Board shall be fixed from
        time to time by resolution of the Board, but in no event shall be less than one (1),
        unless a greater minimum number is required by law. Directors need not be
        shareholders of the Corporation unless otherwise required by resolution of the Board
        or the Certificate of Incorporation.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 4.3 Election and Term.</span>
        Directors shall be elected at each annual meeting of shareholders by the holders of
        shares entitled to vote thereon. Each director shall hold office until the next
        annual meeting of shareholders and until such director’s successor shall have been
        duly elected and qualified, or until such director’s earlier resignation, removal,
        or death.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 4.4 Regular Meetings.</span>
        Regular meetings of the Board may be held at such times and places as may from time
        to time be determined by resolution of the Board or by the Chair of the Board. No
        additional notice of such regular meetings shall be required other than such
        resolution or entry in the minutes of the Board.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 4.5 Special Meetings.</span>
        Special meetings of the Board may be called at any time by the Chair of the Board,
        the CEO, or any two (2) directors then in office. Notice of any special meeting of
        the Board shall be given to each director at least twenty-four (24) hours prior to
        the meeting, either personally, by telephone, by electronic mail, or by other form of
        electronic transmission, or on such shorter or longer notice as may be approved by
        the directors.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 4.6 Quorum and Voting.</span>
        Except as otherwise required by law, the Certificate of Incorporation, or these
        Bylaws, a majority of the directors then in office shall constitute a quorum for the
        transaction of business at any meeting of the Board. The act of a majority of the
        directors present at a meeting at which a quorum is present shall be the act of the
        Board.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 4.7 Action Without Meeting.</span>
        Unless otherwise restricted by the Certificate of Incorporation or these Bylaws, any
        action required or permitted to be taken at any meeting of the Board or of any
        committee thereof may be taken without a meeting if all members of the Board or such
        committee, as the case may be, consent thereto in writing or by electronic
        transmission, and such writing or writings or electronic transmissions are filed
        with the minutes of proceedings of the Board or committee.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 4.8 Committees.</span>
        The Board may, by resolution adopted by a majority of the directors then in office,
        designate one or more committees, each committee to consist of one or more of the
        directors of the Corporation. Any such committee, to the extent provided in such
        resolution and not restricted by law, the Certificate of Incorporation, or these
        Bylaws, shall have and may exercise all the powers and authority of the Board in the
        management of the business and affairs of the Corporation.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 4.9 Resignation and Removal.</span>
        Any director may resign at any time upon written or electronic notice to the Board,
        the Chair of the Board, or the Secretary. Such resignation shall take effect at the
        time specified therein, or, if no time is specified, upon receipt. Any director or
        the entire Board may be removed, with or without cause, by the holders of a majority
        of the shares then entitled to vote at an election of directors, except as otherwise
        provided by the DGCL, the Certificate of Incorporation, or any applicable agreement.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ARTICLE V -->
    <div class="article page-break">
      <h3>ARTICLE V – OFFICERS</h3>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 5.1 Officers.</span>
        The officers of the Corporation shall include, at a minimum, a Chief Executive
        Officer (“CEO”), a Chief Financial Officer (“CFO”), a Chief Technology Officer
        (“CTO”), and a Secretary. The Corporation may also have such other officers,
        including without limitation a Chief Experience Officer (“CXO”), a President, one or
        more Vice Presidents, Assistant Secretaries, Assistant Treasurers, or other
        executive or administrative officers, as the Board may from time to time determine.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 5.2 Appointment; Initial Officers.</span>
        The officers of the Corporation shall be appointed by the Board and shall hold office
        at the pleasure of the Board and until their successors are duly appointed and
        qualified or until their earlier resignation, removal, or death. As of the adoption
        of these Bylaws, the Corporation recognizes the following initial officers:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Chief Executive Officer:</strong> {{ceo_name}}</li>
        <li><strong>Chief Financial Officer:</strong> {{cfo_name}}</li>
        <li><strong>Chief Technology Officer:</strong> {{cxo_name}}</li>
        <li><strong>Secretary:</strong> {{secretary_name}} ({{secretary_title}})</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 5.3 Removal.</span>
        Any officer may be removed, either with or without cause, by the Board at any time,
        without prejudice to the contractual rights, if any, of the person so removed. The
        appointment of an officer shall not of itself create contractual rights.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 5.4 Chief Executive Officer.</span>
        The CEO shall be the chief executive officer of the Corporation and, subject to the
        control and oversight of the Board, shall have general and active supervision,
        direction, and control over the business, properties, and affairs of the
        Corporation. The CEO shall have the authority to implement and enforce executive
        performance standards, meeting attendance requirements, and operational directives
        consistent with these Bylaws and with any resolutions or policies adopted by the
        Board.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 5.5 Chief Financial Officer.</span>
        The CFO shall be the chief financial officer of the Corporation and shall be
        responsible for all financial matters of the Corporation, including without
        limitation budgeting, accounting, financial reporting, treasury functions, and
        oversight of financial controls, subject to the authority of the CEO and the Board.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 5.6 Chief Technology Officer.</span>
        The CTO shall be the senior executive officer responsible for the technology
        strategy, architecture, product and platform engineering, and technical operations
        of the Corporation. The CTO shall oversee the design, development, security,
        maintenance, and scalability of the Corporation’s technology stack, including all
        software, systems, and AI or automation infrastructure deployed in connection with
        the Corporation’s business, subject to the direction of the CEO and the Board.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 5.7 Other Officers.</span>
        The Board may appoint such other officers as it deems necessary or appropriate for
        the conduct of the Corporation’s business, who shall have such titles, authority,
        and responsibilities as may be determined from time to time by the Board or the CEO.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 5.8 Secretary.</span>
        The Secretary shall attend all meetings of the Board and, where requested, of the
        shareholders, and shall maintain or cause to be maintained minutes of such meetings
        in the corporate records. The Secretary shall be the custodian of the corporate
        seal, if any, and of the Corporation’s minute books, stock books, and other records,
        and shall give or cause to be given all notices required by law or by these Bylaws.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ARTICLE VI -->
    <div class="article">
      <h3>ARTICLE VI – INDEMNIFICATION</h3>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 6.1 Indemnification.</span>
        To the fullest extent permitted by the DGCL, the Corporation shall indemnify any
        person who is or was a director or officer of the Corporation, or who is or was
        serving at the request of the Corporation as a director, officer, employee, or agent
        of another corporation, partnership, joint venture, trust, or other enterprise,
        against any and all expenses (including attorneys’ fees), judgments, fines, and
        amounts paid in settlement actually and reasonably incurred by such person in
        connection with any threatened, pending, or completed action, suit, or proceeding,
        whether civil, criminal, administrative, or investigative, to which such person is
        or was a party by reason of the fact that such person is or was in any such capacity.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 6.2 Advancement of Expenses.</span>
        Expenses (including attorneys’ fees) incurred by an indemnified person in defending
        or investigating a proceeding shall be advanced by the Corporation prior to the final
        disposition of such proceeding upon receipt of an undertaking by or on behalf of such
        person to repay such amount if it shall ultimately be determined that such person is
        not entitled to be indemnified by the Corporation.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 6.3 Non-Exclusivity.</span>
        The right to indemnification and advancement of expenses conferred by this Article
        shall not be exclusive of any other right which any person may have or hereafter
        acquire under any statute, the Certificate of Incorporation, these Bylaws, agreement,
        vote of shareholders or disinterested directors, or otherwise.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ARTICLE VII -->
    <div class="article">
      <h3>ARTICLE VII – CORPORATE RECORDS AND SEAL</h3>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 7.1 Records.</span>
        The Corporation shall maintain accurate and complete books and records of account,
        minutes of the proceedings of its shareholders, the Board, and committees of the
        Board, and a record of its shareholders, all in such form and manner as required by
        law.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 7.2 Corporate Seal.</span>
        The Corporation may adopt a corporate seal in such form as the Board may determine,
        but the absence of a seal shall not affect the validity of any instrument executed on
        behalf of the Corporation.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ARTICLE VIII -->
    <div class="article">
      <h3>ARTICLE VIII – CONTRACTS, CHECKS, AND TRANSFERS</h3>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 8.1 Contracts.</span>
        The Board may authorize any officer or officers, or any agent or agents, to enter
        into any contract or execute and deliver any instrument in the name and on behalf of
        the Corporation, and such authority may be general or confined to specific instances.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 8.2 Checks and Drafts.</span>
        All checks, drafts, or other orders for the payment of money, notes, or other
        evidences of indebtedness issued in the name of the Corporation shall be signed by
        such officer or officers, agent or agents of the Corporation and in such manner as
        shall from time to time be determined by resolution of the Board.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 8.3 Transfer of Securities.</span>
        Any shares or other securities owned by the Corporation may be transferred, assigned,
        or endorsed for transfer on behalf of the Corporation by such officer or officers or
        agent or agents as the Board may authorize.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ARTICLE IX -->
    <div class="article">
      <h3>ARTICLE IX – FISCAL YEAR</h3>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 9.1 Fiscal Year.</span>
        The fiscal year of the Corporation shall be fixed by resolution of the Board and may
        be changed from time to time by the Board as it deems appropriate.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ARTICLE X -->
    <div class="article">
      <h3>ARTICLE X – AMENDMENTS</h3>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 10.1 Amendments by the Board.</span>
        The Board shall have the power to adopt, amend, or repeal these Bylaws, subject to
        any limitations set forth in the Certificate of Incorporation, these Bylaws, or
        applicable law.
      </p>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 10.2 Amendments by Shareholders.</span>
        The shareholders may adopt, amend, or repeal these Bylaws by the affirmative vote of
        the holders of a majority of the shares entitled to vote thereon, unless a greater
        vote is required by law, the Certificate of Incorporation, or these Bylaws.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ARTICLE XI -->
    <div class="article">
      <h3>ARTICLE XI – GOVERNING LAW</h3>

      <p class="block">
        <span class="section-title">Section 11.1 Governing Law.</span>
        These Bylaws and the interpretation thereof shall be governed by and construed in
        accordance with the laws of the State of {{governing_law}}, without regard to conflict-of-laws
        principles.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="signature-section page-break">
      <p class="execution-note">
        IN WITNESS WHEREOF, the undersigned, being all of the duly appointed and acting
        members of the Board of Directors of {{company_name}}, hereby adopt the foregoing
        Bylaws as the Bylaws of the Corporation, effective as of {{adoption_date}}.
      </p>

      {{{signers}}}

      <p class="execution-note">
        Executed and acknowledged via the {{company_name}} Executive Portal e-signature workflow.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
